<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oreste Baratieri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1841">1841</a>–<a href="/years/1901">1901</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oreste Baratieri (1841–1901) was an Italian general who had fought with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-garibaldi">Garibaldi</a>'s Thousand and became governor of the colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a> in the early 1890s. Commanding the Italian army in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-italo-ethiopian-war">First Italo-Ethiopian War</a>, he was decisively defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-adwa">Battle of Adwa</a> on 1 March 1896. The disaster ended his career, brought down the Crispi government and secured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>'s independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oreste-baratieri.jpg" alt="Oreste Baratieri" width="227" height="355" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown, but died more than 70 years ago · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oreste_Baratieri.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
